  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Suppose the point $P(x,y)$ is located at an equal distance from points $A(3,1)$ and $B(-1,3)$. Find a formula for $y$ in terms of $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=2x$.\n\nEquate the squared distances $PA^2$ and $PB^2$.",
      "worked": "Since $PA=PB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}PA^2&=PB^2\\\\(x-3)^2+(y-1)^2&=(x+1)^2+(y-3)^2\\\\x^2-6x+9+y^2-2y+1&=x^2+2x+1+y^2-6y+9\\\\-6x-2y&=2x-6y\\\\4y&=8x\\\\y&=2x\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
